  "Scenes.Marblescene.ExtendedMurbelFarmTalkz.MarbleDoubleTake": "[pg]Marble starts, realizing that she'd been staring wistfully off into space, then she makes a double take and looks out the window. [say: I'm sorry sweetie, but I forgot Whitney had a job for me that I need to go help her with. Why don't we finish this some other time?] She seems in a hurry to go, so you bid the friendly cow-girl good day and return to your camp."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.ExtendedMurbelFarmTalkz.MarbleNotesMission": "Marble looks over you a moment before saying, [say: You've mentioned this 'mission' a few times now; I guess that's why you left home?] You nod. [say: Fulfilling a duty, huh? My story isn't quite the same as yours, and certainly not so noble!] She laughs at this."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.ExtendedMurbelFarmTalkz.MarbleOffersOwnTale": "After telling Marble about your explorations of the world thus far, Marble offers to tell you a bit more about her own journey. [say: My family actually lives on the other side of the mountains to the south.] She pauses, then chuckles. [say: Or is it to the north? You know how hard it is to describe direction over long distances, don't you?] You nod; while you've never had any problem with it back home, you can well imagine how the magic of this realm would eliminate the need for such facility."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.ExtendedMurbelFarmTalkz.MealPassesQuietly": "[pg]The rest of the meal passes without anything of interest being discussed. Having now finished your meal together, the two of you stand up and Marble shows you out of her room. As you're leaving, Marble tells you with a smile on her face that she enjoyed your talk together, and hopes that you'll join her for another soon."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.ExtendedMurbelFarmTalkz.MissedNursingAnsgar": " After my falling out with Ansgar, I noticed that I really missed nursing him more than anything else.[sayend] She stops for a moment, shaking her head. [say: That's not quite right. It's more that I needed to keep nursing; it just felt like everything was wrong with me if I wasn't nursing something.]"
