  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsMeetEdrynFuckbuddy.TooManyChildrenStrain": ", and moving so many children to live here at once would be a strain on the town. Edryn understands your reasoning, though she maintains her position."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.AwareOfSpiceHerbs": "[pg]You're well aware of which herbs Marble usually uses as spices and mostly keep to it, through you also gather others you think are safe, wondering if she'd be able to make something of them."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.BothWord": "both"
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.BrokenStructureCry": "[pg][say: Mommy, it broke again!]"
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.CanManageProtest": "[pg][say: S... Sweetie, I can take care of things. I know you're busy doing other important...]"
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.DaughterClopsIntoArms": "Your daughter immediately clops up to you and jumps into your arms. [say: {0}! Play with me!] You laugh at the girl in your arms, so young and yet full of energy. She proceeds to rope you into a grand adventure, where you play the parts of the one who searches for a hero to save their camp, and the monster that has to be stopped, and also the monster's hostage that needs to be saved, while she is the great bovine savior that carries out this grand quest."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.EagerKidQuestion": "[pg][say: {0}! Is this it? Is this it?]"
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.EnergeticGrabbingKids": "[pg]They're certainly very energetic but have a tendency to simply grab things and ask you if they're the good ones rather than simply gathering what you instruct them to gather. You swear one has picked out something that looks almost like a poisonous toadstool from your home, and yet another brought you a Whisker Fruit. You gently collect them and send the kids back out, then quietly dispose of all the hazardous items. This continues for a while, but eventually your basket is full."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.GameEndsBovineTriumph": "[pg]The game finally ends with the bovine savior victorious over the horde of ravenous monsters - somewhere along the line it was decided that hostages were no fun and single combat wasn't impressive enough, and you exhausted your theatrical skills to provide a bevy of satisfyingly scary faces and growls - and the people of the land (you) rejoicing. You're left a bit tired afterwards, but you certainly don't regret having played with your child."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.GameEndsBovineVictory": "[pg]The game finally ends with the bovine savior victorious over the horde of ravenous monsters - somewhere along the line it was decided that hostages were no fun and single combat wasn't impressive enough, and you exhausted your theatrical skills to provide a bevy of satisfyingly scary faces and growls - and the people of the land (you) rejoicing. You're left a bit tired afterwards, but you certainly don't regret having played with your child."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.GatherReturnToCamp": "[pg]Having gathered the things that looked like they were what Marble might need, you return to camp."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.HalfOfYourChildren": "about half of your children"
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.HourNearlyUpGoodbye": "[pg]When the hour is nearly up, you tell your offspring that it is time to wind down and get ready to leave. There are some protests, but they don't last long when Whitney promises a treat to each of them as they leave. She goes off into the kitchen briefly, and when you've got the girls all ready to leave, she reappears with a tray of muffins, one for each child. It is with smiling faces full of baked goodness that your kids return to camp."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.JoinHerWithKids": "[pg]You join her with the kids and help keep them under control while they play with their Auntie and the toy she's made them. As tiring as it is for the canine farmer, you can tell that she loves spending time with these kids and listening to their excited voices call her <i>Auntie</i>."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.KidsGreetAtNursery": "When you approach the nursery, the faces of your kids immediately light up and as one they cry out, [say: {0}! Tell us a story!] They crowd around you, excited at the prospect of hearing of your adventures. It would seem that, once again, the kids will be the ones that decide what will be happening in your time with them."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.KnowsSpicesByHeart": "[pg]You know Marble's [say: spices] by heart and are well aware of what here can also be used as these. Gathering them all with your children, you return to camp well-stuffed with them."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.LiftsYouBigHug": "grabs you and immediately lifts you up to her chest, giving you a big hug."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.LoveYouThanks": "[pg][say: Thank you sweetie. I love you.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.MarbleAsksWhitneyVisit": "Marble calls you over and asks that you take the kids to visit with Whitney - she'd like to do some things around camp while they aren't around. You nod and turn to your children and tell them it is time to go and visit Auntie Whitney. [say: Yay!] they shout and all start to crowd around. You inform Marble that you'll be back in an hour, and proceed to the farm with your children, the youngest one holding your hand shyly."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.MarblePatienceLessons": "[pg]With infinite motherly patience, Marble sits down next to your children and again shows them how to make the basic supports. You smile before departing to continue with your other work."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.MarbleSitsOnLogs": "You notice Marble is sitting on some wood logs with your children. Curious, you decide to check what exactly is going on."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.MarbleTeachesBuilding": "[pg]Apparently, Marble is attempting to teach your children how to properly create wooden structures, starting by constructing small 'houses' and little toys from several pieces of wood. It would appear "
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.MarbleWaitsRested": "[pg]Approaching the camp, Marble is already waiting for you and seems a lot more relaxed and rested. Taking the baskets with the herbs from you, she beams you a beautiful smile, then "
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.MarbleWearySmile": "Marble looks up when you approach and gives you a weary smile. [say: Hello, sweetie.]"
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.QuickTravelToWhitney": "[pg]Thanks to the queer nature of travel in this land, it takes you no time at all to arrive at the edge of Whitney's peaceful island in the demon-blight. Before long, the girls start to run ahead, eagerly anticipating the visit with the southern belle. By the time you arrive at Whitney's house, she's already let the mini-Marbles inside, and is entertaining them in her sitting room. There is an excited cry when she presents them with her latest homemade toy."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.SkipsExplicitParts": " You do make sure to skip over the items of a more explicit nature throughout."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.SomeKnackForIt": " have at least some knack for it."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.SonClopsIntoArms": "Your son immediately clops up to you and jumps into your arms. [say: {0}! Play with me!] You laugh at the boy in your arms, so young and yet full of energy. He proceeds to rope you into a grand adventure, where you play the parts of the one who searches for a hero to save their camp, and the monster that has to be stopped, and also the monster's hostage that needs to be saved, while she is the great bovine savior that carries out this grand quest."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.StoryEndsFarewell": " Eventually your story comes to an end, and you bid farewell to your kids."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.StrongWarmEmbrace": "embraces you strongly, pressing her warm body against yours."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.TaleOfExploits": "[pg]You launch into another tale of your exploits (that may or may not have actually happened to you) much to the enjoyment of your little ones. They listen with rapt attention and smiles on their faces as you talk of your successes, worried looks when you sound like you might be in danger, and great cheers when you do make it out all right."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.ThankfulForRest": "[pg][say: Thank you. You really are amazing. Well, I certainly could use a rest... And we still have to get some stuff done for dinner, so if you could take them and gather some herbs as spice, it would both give them something to do and be greatly helpful.]"
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.TiredKidsAfterWork": "[pg]Your kids are just a little bit tired from all the work and it doesn't seem they'll pester Marble much more today. One of them even grabs you, complaining, [say: {0}, I'm sleepy!] You pat her head and smile, telling her that you'll be home soon enough."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.YouCallTheBrood": "[pg]With a nod, you call your brood and announce that all of you will be gathering some important plants for Mommy Marble. The kids swarm around you and just the walk to the edge of the forest is enough for you to notice how tiring it can be dealing with all of them."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.YouSilenceHerExplain": "[pg]You silence her and kindly explain that the kids are your own as well as hers, and therefore you also share some of the responsibility for them; moreover, you can't bear to watch her tired all the time from their sheer numbers. She smiles again."
  "Scenes.Marblescene.MarbleKidsPlaytime.YouSmileAndSuggest": "[pg]With a smile of your own, you tell her that she seems a bit too tired to attend your kids for the rest of the day and ask if there's anything you can do to help."
